// Pull request: #6129 Add process creation rule for hidden local user account creation via net.exe
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6129
// Pull request author: KKarishan
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Creation of a Local Hidden User Account by Registry
// Sigma ID: 460479f3-80b7-42da-9c43-2cc1d54dbccd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-05-03 | Modified: 2026-08-21
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1136.001
// Description: Detects creation or modification of local account name entries ending with a dollar sign under
//   the SAM Users Names registry path. This indicates an attempt to creates a hidden local user
//   account, which is a technique used by threat actors to maintain persistence on a compromised
//   system while avoiding detection.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/SBousseaden/status/1387530414185664538
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4dd00b24e0b32f6154064f1313ecea11beaef50e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_add_local_hidden_user.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (ActionType =~ "RegistryKeyCreated" and RegistryKey endswith "$" and RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SAM\\SAM\\Domains\\Account\\Users\\Names.*$") or (ActionType =~ "RegistryValueSet" and RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SAM\\SAM\\Domains\\Account\\Users\\Names.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "$\\(Default)")
